      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T00:35:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ahhhh, indeed. That\u0027s interesting.",
      "parentUuid": "0781cd69_c4525a89",
      "revId": "36da3e4e15f68b87943f209d8d9c9a5a7e9efb34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41ca0368_9caac41a",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/Ikev2VpnProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 734,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T07:01:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you do this, you\u0027ll need to do the opposite in the fromVpnProfile. Otherwise we\u0027ll serialize it as a hex of hte value, and then never un-hex it",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 734,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "36da3e4e15f68b87943f209d8d9c9a5a7e9efb34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c73ddaf9_603d209f",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/Ikev2VpnProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 734,
      "author": {
        "id": 1304263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T12:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We won\u0027t set the server and Identification into the Ikev2VpnProfile in fromVpnProfile() if IkeTunnelConnectionParams is set in the vpnProfile. The value in IkeSessionParams is stored/set as a byte array. I expect that callers should get from IkeTunnelConnectionParams directly(though it really depends on the app side). I did not see it\u0027s clearly defined what format should be return here. It\u0027s actually a confusing API(at least for me).",
      "parentUuid": "41ca0368_9caac41a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 734,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "36da3e4e15f68b87943f209d8d9c9a5a7e9efb34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25d7f63f_9358fb26",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/Ikev2VpnProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 734,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T00:35:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to fix the bug this way, suggest instead of doing this, always hex it in toVpnProfile(), and un-hex it in fromVpnProfile()\n\nThe same format is used by some of the other open source implementations, thus the convolutedness of it.\n\nBut assuming someone sets the KeyIdIdentification, they probably assume they get the equivalvalent value out here as they would if they set the key ID as a string (see VpnIkev2Utils)",
      "parentUuid": "41ca0368_9caac41a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 734,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "36da3e4e15f68b87943f209d8d9c9a5a7e9efb34",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc1ee176_c7fa55fc",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/Ikev2VpnProfile.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 734,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-13T05:34:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay so it sounds like we have a long-standing, huge bug in the existing implementation where we use \\0 as a separator but never care to escape it, instead relying on UI to never supply one which is a terrible idea (and if you\u0027re wondering why, then ponder why we have this bug now. Yeah this kind of thing *always* happens in one shape or another when you rely on what UI can do for correctness).\n\nNow the problem is that we can\u0027t really change this now. Really, we should escape the keyId and all other fields somehow, but to do this in a backward-compatible manner we need to version the file or something and make sure the reading part is always as recent as the writing part.\n\nI don\u0027t think this particular patch is good ; it writes what\u0027s in effect garbage to the string (in that it can\u0027t be interpreted correctly by the reading code) and relies on the reading code never fetching this value. If we\u0027re going to rely on that, I think aosp/2200482 is better because a null value makes it a lot clearer that it shouldn\u0027t be read from here.",
      "parentUuid": "25d7f63f_9358fb26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 734,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "36da3e4e15f68b87943f209d8d9c9a5a7e9efb34",
